{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Let them dwell.</b> The outcasts — the words of the prophet or of HaShem, for the honor of Israel." "<b>Because of the devastator.</b> Who devastated Samaria, and he is the king of Assyria." "<b>For, etc.</b> Yet a time will come when this taskmaster will perish and the devastation will cease." "<b>Who exacts.</b> An adjective describing the noun, and it is derived from the same root as תמוצו (Isaiah 66:11)." "<b>Have ceased.</b> The camps of <b>the trampler</b> — he is the king of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:59.205196123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}